course: dictionary
lesson: 10816
title: Veg: short for vegetables
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Veg is a short, chatty word. It is clipped from vegetable, so people cut off the end and say veg. «Eat your veg!» means eat your vegetables, the green and orange foods on your plate.
explain: Veg is most often a noun. «A fruit and veg stall» is a stall that sells fruit and vegetables, so veg is a kind of food. Read the words around it: they tell you that veg is something you can buy and eat.
explain: Veg can also be a verb, and then it means something very different. To veg out means to relax and do nothing much, like lying on the sofa. The same short word can mean food or lazing about, so always check the clues around it.
fact: Veg is short for vegetable or vegetables. It is informal, so you use it in everyday talk, not in formal writing.
fact: Veg is used mostly in the UK, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «Fruit and veg» means fruit and vegetables together.
fact: «Veg out» means to relax and do nothing much. It is informal slang.
fact: In the Eatwell Guide, about a third of the plate is fruit and veg.
exercise: In «a fruit and veg stall», what does veg mean? | Vegetables, the food | A type of wooden box | A kind of game | *Fruit and vegetables, sold on a stall
exercise: Dad says, «I'm going to veg out on the sofa tonight.» What does veg out mean? | To run very fast | To cook a big dinner | *To relax and do nothing much
exercise: Why is veg called informal? | It is a very old word from a book of rules | It is a formal word used only in science | *It is a short, chatty word used in everyday talk
test: «Fruit and veg of different colours give different vitamins and minerals.» What is the main idea? | Only red fruit is healthy | Veg is not food | *Eating many colours of fruit and veg gives a good mix | Vitamins are found only in sweets
test: Kieran talks about his «veg patch». What is a veg patch? | *A small piece of ground for growing vegetables | A bag for carrying shopping | A place to sleep | A patch of old carpet
exam: «In the Eatwell Guide about a third of the plate is fruit and veg.» What part of the plate is fruit and veg? | Almost all of it | About a half | None of it | *About a third
